WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.291
"The Role of Accountability in Weight Loss"

00:00:07.135 --> 00:00:09.120
Among the more radical
weight loss methods

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.800
that have been employed:

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.120
"therapeutic starvation."

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.880
How can you get people
to stop eating?

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.360
Wire their jaws shut.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.160
Ugh, yes,
that used to be a thing.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.440
Terrible.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.640
I can't even imagine
the psychological toll.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.840
Surgical fixes
like jaw wiring aside,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.160
what is the most effective
long-term obesity program

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.800
ever published
in the medical literature?

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.080
The Trevose Behavior
Modification Program.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.080
Named after a town
in Pennsylvania,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.960
the program ran all-volunteer
self-help support groups

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.040
beginning in 1970,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.480
offering lifetime treatment
at no cost.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.680
Wait, the most successful
weight loss program

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.000
in history was free?

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.760
Why haven't more people
heard about it?

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.720
Probably because of that:

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.320
It was free.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.960
Multimillion dollar corporations
like Weight Watchers

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.853
spend hundreds of millions
of dollars

00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:09.187
on advertising each year.
How do the two programs compare?

00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:10.858
After two years
in Weight Watchers,

00:01:10.858 --> 00:01:13.775
the average weight loss
is about six pounds (2.7 kg).

00:01:13.775 --> 00:01:15.920
After two years
in the Trevose Program,

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.120
the average weight loss
was 39 pounds (17.7 kg),

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.320
and after five years,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.560
Trevose participants were
still down 35 pounds (16 kg).

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.800
Now, that's only
for about the 20%

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.720
who stayed in the program
that long.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.600
What about Weight Watchers
participants?

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.080
After five years
sticking with the most rigorous

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.240
52-week Weight Watchers program,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.520
participants did maintain
a lower weight—

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.676
but only about
five and a half pounds (2.5 kg).

00:01:43.676 --> 00:01:48.240
And drop out, when reported,
averaged around 20%.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.600
What appears to be the secret

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.400
to the Trevose Program's
success?

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.480
Extreme accountability.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.320
The Trevose Program
has been likened

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.080
to "weight-loss boot camp,"

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.840
but the rigor is in the rules,
not the methods.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.920
The program utilizes
the standard array

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.080
of traditional techniques:

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.960
calorie cutting, exercise,
weekly weigh-ins,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.280
and group support.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.320
What sets it apart

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.440
is the strictness
of its enforcement.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.520
If members fail
to attend meetings

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.840
or meet their weight loss goals,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.120
they are immediately kicked out,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.880
and they can never return.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.640
The program accepts
almost anyone

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.880
with one critical exception:

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.920
no past participants
are allowed.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.000
There are no second chances,
no do-overs, no excuses.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.240
When people sign up,
they understand that this is

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.440
a once-in-a-lifetime
opportunity.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.000
Unfortunately,
the program closed in 2021

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.400
due to the challenges
of hosting in-person groups

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.280
during the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.520
Trevose's tough love approach
may not be for everyone,

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.800
but key principles for success,
such as social support,

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.800
may be universal.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.200
A randomized trial
found that group therapy

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.800
tends to produce
greater results

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.800
than going it on our own,

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.480
even among those
who initially expressed

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.760
a preference
for individual treatment.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.080
Similarly, health coaches
can also help people

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.560
stay engaged and accountable.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.600
Self-monitoring is
another important takeaway,

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.760
considered the "cornerstone"
of behavioral change

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.320
for weight loss.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.000
Without awareness
of our progress,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.040
it may be hard
to reach our goals.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.280
There are now high-tech
wearable activity trackers

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.480
to monitor our exercise
to facilitate weight loss,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.200
but the best device
for monitoring calorie intake

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.080
may be
the humble bathroom scale.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.480
In the past, though,
frequent self-weighing

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.440
for weight control
was actively discouraged.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.400
Clinicians were concerned
dieters might be discouraged

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.000
by the slow rate
of weight loss,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.680
or worse, suffer
negative psychological effects,

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.600
potentially putting one at risk
for depression

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.240
or body image issues.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.240
Self-weighing may indeed
have a negative impact

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.360
for adolescents and adults
without excess weight,

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.880
but daily or weekly
self-weighing

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.560
among adults who are overweight
or adults with obesity

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.880
appears to actually improve
psychological health

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.880
and well-being.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.560
Among those
who need to lose weight,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.400
self-weighing is
broadly positive:

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.000
associated with less depression,

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.280
disordered eating,
and body dissatisfaction.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.040
But this may be confounded
by the fact

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.400
that regular self-weighing
improves weight loss.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.040
Findings from more than a dozen
such prospective studies

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.360
have consistently found
regular self-weighing

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.280
to be associated
with successful weight loss

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.760
and maintenance,
but they are all stricken

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.840
with the same nagging question.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.120
It's unknown whether those
who weigh themselves daily

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.040
are more motivated
to lose weight

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.160
and, therefore, more likely

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.040
to weigh themselves
more frequently

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.120
or whether frequent
self-weighing

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.960
sparks behavior change
that leads to weight loss.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.760
Or maybe there's
a third factor at play.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.200
You can't prove
cause and effect

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.520
until you put it to the test.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.040
Randomized controlled trials
have shown

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.720
that those assigned
to daily weighing

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.120
accompanied
by weekly email messaging

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.400
tailored to their progress
lost more weight,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.560
about six percent more.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.120
They were better able
to resist weight gain

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.760
and maintained
more weight loss.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.520
The control groups
received nothing, though;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.760
so, it's hard to separate
the effects of the weighing

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.440
from the regular contact.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.600
Just telling individuals
with obesity

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.800
to weigh themselves each day

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.800
without any further instruction
or feedback

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.000
is ineffective
as a sole strategy.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.440
Self-monitoring has been shown

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.680
to be an effective
behavioral technique

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.600
for helping people eat
more healthfully,

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.720
exercise more,
and drink less alcohol.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.240
But unlike those cases,

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.720
self-weighing is monitoring
an outcome

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.280
rather than specific behaviors.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.280
If people don't know
what to do about the fact

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.000
they're gaining weight,
it may not help.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.680
Self-weighing is
just a feedback tool

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.760
to allow
for personal accountability,

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.840
offering positive
or negative reinforcement

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.600
for whatever strategies
you've chosen to try out.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.520
The evidence supporting
frequent self-weighing

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.120
as a part of weight management
interventions

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.760
is now considered so strong
that it's been incorporated

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.600
into the official
weight management guidelines

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.760
put out by the Obesity Society,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.680
along with the American
Heart Association

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.080
and the American College
of Cardiology

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.840
and as part
of their most recent guidelines

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.280
for the prevention
of heart disease

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.280
among people who are overweight
or who have obesity.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.640
So, how often
should we weigh ourselves?

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.840
There is insufficient evidence

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.560
to support a specific
frequency of weighing,

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.480
whether weekly or daily.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.160
One study found
that twice daily—

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.800
upon waking
and again right before bed—

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.200
appeared superior to once a day,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.120
about six pounds (2.7 kg)
versus two pounds (0.9 kg)

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.520
of weight loss
over 12 weeks;

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.000
so, that's the frequency
recommended by Dr. Greger

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.240
in his book
on evidence-based weight loss,

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.000
How Not to Diet.

